  "explicit_limitations": [
    "Prefill-isolation protocol: each request generates only 1 output token on a single 48 GB A6000 P/D prefill node; reported TTFT tail/median ratios do not establish full multi-turn agent workflow JCT gains.",
    "Trace approximations: RAG workloads synthesize Zipf (alpha=0.9) popularity and Poisson arrivals plus crafted bursts; Mooncake traces keep 1 in 8 sessions, scale prompt lengths by 1/4, and time-compress native rho=0.8 to 0.9 and 1.1.",
    "Median latency cost regimes: under persistent overload with shallow reuse (MuSiQue rho=1.1), Fairway median TTFT rises to 3.0s vs LPM 0.9s (for lowest p99 12.62s vs 14.2s); under flood stress, cached hits wait at 18.2s median while backlog drains.",
    "One-step work-charge bound covers oldest requests up to ~w*B (~8k tokens at w=4, B=2,048) assuming budget and KV headroom without self-eviction; larger prompts rely on relative-wait aging, est(len_r) assumes static idle prefill timing, and no official code repository is linked in v1."
  ],
